Z||000005||Sage||11-15-2001||12:08 PM||||What do I call goat meat?<P>Off limits!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Edited to add:<P>Don't like chicken either.  Or rattlesnake, or alligator or flounder!  You know what they say...to each his own.  Course, if you eat at McDonalds, you don't know what you've had!  They were makin deer burgers here one year, before that it was kangaroo.<P>Back on topic, I believe goat "tripe" is the stomache.  I think that term is used for the stomache of any animal.  Oh yea, don't do head cheese either. <P>I knew a farmer here that used everything from the cows they slaughtered.  They even made blood pudding.  Think that is common practice among the Amish too.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!<p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||1
