Z||000016||maryjane||11-15-2001||10:08 PM||||Not much I've not eaten, here or overseas. Most memorable for the bad taste and smell was a baloot, in the Philipines. It is a half incubated duck egg. Ate monkey-meat on a stick. Barbecued  on a brazier by a street vendor. Then when I was in Thailand, I ordered a 'haahm-buhga' as they called it. (hamburger). It was incredibly lean and bland. Found out a few minutes later, it was monkey meat. A couple of Thai citizens were eating at a table nearby, with a hole in the middle, eating something from the hole. There was a terrible screeching going on, you can guess what the main course was. Found this picture of a baloot. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wwye1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
