Z||000031||WampusCat||11-19-2001||08:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>If you ever order the "menudo" in a mexican restaurant, you will be getting tripe-that is, stomach.<P>Sweetbreads are pancreas or esophagus.  Wonder how they got that name.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>When we went desert camping in AZ, we always cooked chorizo and potatoes for breakfast.  I made the mistake of reading the ingredients label on the chorizo once: "saliva glands, lymph nodes, fat, spices." yum!  I lived in Eagle Pass, TX for a couple of years too, that's where I had cabrito and menudo.||||reg||1
